# CODEOWNERS for SoloGam/worldforge-app
#
# A record of who owns the security-sensitive paths, and a way to get
# @SoloGam auto-requested as reviewer on any PR (including Dependabot's) that
# touches them. Code-owner review is NOT required: the "main protection"
# ruleset sets require_code_owner_review=false and 0 required approvals, so
# this file never blocks a merge on its own. Revisit that if outside
# contributors or other accounts with merge rights are added.
#
# Later matching lines take precedence over earlier ones; every line here has
# the same owner, so the order only matters for readability.

# CI workflows, Dependabot config and this file itself.
/.github/                       @SoloGam

# gitleaks: the reviewed config is the only allowed exception path.
/.gitleaks.toml                 @SoloGam
# CI fails on any tracked .gitleaksignore; own them anywhere so one in a PR is noticed.
.gitleaksignore                 @SoloGam

# Git attributes change how files are checked out and diffed (the mod-source
# byte-exact check, and the gitleaks history scan's view of past commits).
.gitattributes                  @SoloGam

# Auth: the whole directory (shared live-preview client, server-side fallback,
# session verification, middleware, and anything added there later).
/src/lib/auth/                  @SoloGam

# Mod-source sync check (script + test): the gate keeping worldforge-mod/, the
# 0.4.0 zip and MOD_SOURCE identical. `*` matches within a file name
# (gitignore syntax, supported by CODEOWNERS).
/scripts/check-mod-source-sync*.mjs @SoloGam

# Dependencies and the Node version: supply chain and Dependabot PRs.
/package.json                   @SoloGam
/package-lock.json              @SoloGam
/.nvmrc                         @SoloGam
